## 8. THINGS I COULD NOT REACH

- **Freed et al., "A Stalker's Paradise" (CHI 2018, DOI 10.1145/3173574.3174241)** — closed access, no Wayback PDF, no OA mirror. Not read.
- **Slupska & Tanczer (2021, DOI 10.1108/978-1-83982-848-520211049)** — CC-BY per Semantic Scholar, but Emerald served HTML instead of the PDF. Metadata only; full text not read. The "multi-user problem" framing attributed to them in the task brief is therefore **unverified here**.
- **Tseng et al.** — no specific work identified or fetched.
- **Bellini's other work on financial coercive control** — not searched (OpenAlex quota exhausted mid-session: `"Rate limit exceeded... Insufficient budget... Resets at midnight UTC"`).
- **CDT live site** — 403 to this environment throughout; all CDT content above came from Wayback copies of the original PDFs.
- **`support.google.com/a/` and `support.google.com/vault/` live** — Google served `google.com/sorry` CAPTCHA; all Workspace content above came from Wayback (dates given per page).
- **Apple Business Manager live guide** — every article now returns only "Apple Business Manager is now Apple Business"; the successor guide at `/guide/apple-business/` is 404. Content from Wayback 2026-03-29. **The rename is in flight as of 2026-09-04** and the Managed Apple Account authority model may change with it.
- **Apple "What Managed Apple Accounts can't access"** article body — referenced, not fetched.
- **Google Security Checkup scope** — no Wayback capture of `accounts/answer/9924334`; live blocked.
- **IIW session notes**, **Sovrin Guardianship Implementation Guidelines V1 / Technical Requirements V1** — no resolvable URLs.
- **Any specific named lawsuit or news incident of a Google Workspace *admin* (as opposed to monitoring software) outing a student** — not found. The documented harm channel is monitoring software running on the managed account, not an admin's manual action.
